{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The threshold showing is made out on this trip and nowhere else. trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip identifier TRP-00111 and agree on the pickup/start at 2026-08-03T07:47:40+08:00, so POL-RD-08(a) is satisfied; and on the trace figure that governs under POL-RD-01 (trace_distance_km 29.98, not the rounded actual_distance_km 30.0) the excess over the booked optimal of 24.0 km is 5.98 km and 24.92% — past both the 0.8 km and the 20% gates. The burden therefore shifts to the driver under POL-RD-08, and the driver discharges it the way that clause requires: by pointing to a specific artifact and a specific clause, not by a general assertion that traffic was bad.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00111", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-FARE-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess is exonerated outright under POL-RD-03. The artefact is EV-ADVIS-00111-01, an LTA DataMall CLOSURE on the 'Pan Island Expressway (PIE) towards Tuas, after Clementi Rd exit' — a segment the booked optimal route uses (the trip record's optimal_route_source is 'BKE southbound then PIE westbound'), so limb (a) is met. Its validity window is 07:10–09:30, bracketing the 07:47:40–08:25:40 trip by far more than the 15-minute buffer limb (b) allows, with 41.5 minutes of overlap and overlaps_trip_window true. The 10-second, 100%-coverage trace on EV-GPS-00111 shows the vehicle leaving the optimal corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed segment and rejoining it on the AYE, which is limb (c). All three conditions are satisfied.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.intersects_route",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The exoneration is not merely partial — it covers the whole measured excess. The POL-RD-03 cap is 1.30 x the ADDITIONAL distance of the shortest lawful alternative over the booked optimal, plus 1.0 km of tolerance: 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km. The measured excess is 5.98 km, which is less than 7.76 km, so justified_excess_km is the measured figure itself and there is no unexonerated residue left for POL-RD-02 to operate on.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-GPS-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.cap_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The routing is the authority's own diversion, not a discretionary shortcut: the advisory text on EV-ADVIS-00111-01 reads 'Diversion via Upper Bukit Timah Rd', which is exactly the road the rider's own claim text describes the driver using ('came off at Bukit Panjang and went down Upper Bukit Timah and around by the AYE'). The driver took the published way round a HIGH-severity closure of the corridor the optimal route uses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Run POL-RD-02 against the closure-adjusted optimal that POL-RD-03 requires — 24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km, duration scaled from the booked 30.0 min to 37.5 min — and the money simply is not there: recomputed_fare = 3.80 + 0.75 x 29.98 + 0.28 x 37.5 + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 37.585, against a charged_total of 37.74. The difference is SGD 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so under POL-RD-02 read with POL-RD-03 the outcome is NO_ACTION and the charged fare of SGD 37.74 stands as recorded on EV-FARE-00111 (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.closure.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no pass-through correction to add on top. EV-FARE-00111 records tolls_erp 0.00 and an empty erp_gantries list, and the trace crosses no gantry, so the standalone off-route ERP refund that POL-RD-09 gives even an exonerated closure has nothing to operate on and the SGD 12.00 cap on that head is not reached. The distance and time charges stand because POL-RD-03 places the closure beyond the driver's control, and the rider's own claim that he 'did not see any closure' does not put a gantry on the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log confirms the driver told the rider before he diverted — MSG-00111-001, sent 07:54:20, 'boss PIE towards tuas closed, lorry fire. i come off at bukit panjang ok' — and the rider read it and answered at 07:54:55, 'as long as i reach by 8.30', without objecting to the route. I do not put this forward as a rider-instructed detour and do not rely on POL-RD-04, because the rider requested no waypoint and waypoint_hint is null; it is offered as contemporaneous notice that corroborates the driver's account of why he left the corridor and rebuts any suggestion the diversion was concealed or self-serving.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation scrutiny is engaged. POL-RD-06 is triggered only by a MATERIAL deviation — excess over 50% of optimal or over 8.0 km absolute, on the excess REMAINING after adjustment — and after the POL-RD-03 cap is applied there is no remaining excess at all, while the raw figures (24.92%, 5.98 km) sit below both materiality thresholds. Were the profile consulted, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 588, which establishes no pattern on the test POL-RD-06 actually states.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00111", "EV-GPS-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.thresholds.material_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the trip's own telemetry shows the route really was longer than booked. EV-GPS-00111 records 29.98 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 24.0 km — an excess of 5.98 km, 24.9%, past both POL-RD-01 gates (0.8 km and 20%). I use the trace figure, which governs, not the rounded 30.0 km convenience copy on EV-TRIP-00111. The threshold is therefore made out and the burden shifts to the driver under POL-RD-08. The driver is nonetheless excused under POL-RD-03. EV-ADVIS-00111-01 is an LTA DataMall closure of the PIE towards Tuas after Clementi Rd — a segment the booked optimal route uses (BKE southbound then PIE westbound); it ran 07:10–09:30, bracketing the 07:47:40–08:25:40 trip; and the trace leaves that corridor at Bukit Panjang before the closed stretch and rejoins it on the AYE afterwards. LTA's own diversion published with the advisory is 'via Upper Bukit Timah Rd' — the road the driver took. I do not accept the rider's argument that the rejoin on the AYE defeats limb (c): one-north is not on the PIE, the optimal route must leave the PIE to reach it, and the trace shows the vehicle leaving the corridor before the closed segment and coming back onto the corridor after it — which is precisely the pattern limb (c) describes. The excuse is capped at the lesser of the measured excess and 1.30 × (29.2 − 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km, so the whole 5.98 km is justified and the closure-adjusted optimal is 29.98 km / 37.5 min. On that adjusted route, POL-RD-02 gives recomputed_fare = 3.80 + 0.75 × 29.98 + 0.28 × 37.5 + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 37.585, against charged_total 37.74 on EV-FARE-00111. The refund is 0.155, below the 0.50 de minimis, so no refund issues and the 37.74 charge stands. The rider's alternative figure of 6.74 (6.75 rounded up) is correct arithmetic against the booked route, but the booked route is not the baseline once POL-RD-03 excuses the excess. No pass-through correction is due: tolls_erp is 0.00 and erp_gantries is empty, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to settle. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (229 fixes at 10 s, no gaps), so it decides the deviation on its own and needs no independent corroboration. No repeat-deviation pattern is engaged, so no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises, and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The rider's 'I did not see any closure' is an assertion with no artifact behind it and does not outweigh the LTA advisory; the driver announced the diversion in the chat at 07:54:20 and the rider answered at 07:54:55 without objecting. On this rider-filed dispute, NO_ACTION leaves the charge as it stands: the SGD 37.74 fare is not refunded, and the SGD 8.00 in dispute is neither returned nor written off."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: this decides DSP-00111 on trip TRP-00111 (Woodlands to one-north, 3 Aug 2026; SGD 37.74 charged). The outcome is NO_ACTION — the fare stands and no money moves.\n\nTHE DEVIATION IS MEASURED, AND THE RIDER'S FIGURES ARE RIGHT. POL-RD-01 makes the GPS trace figure (29.98 km on EV-GPS-00111), not the rounded 30.0 km on the trip record, the governing measurement. Against the booked optimal of 24.0 km that is an excess of 5.98 km, or 24.92% — past both the 0.8 km and the 20% gates — so a deviation is established, and the burden shifted to the driver under POL-RD-08. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07: 229 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and no jumps, so the deviation stands on the trace alone.\n\nTHAT DEVIATION IS FULLY EXONERATED UNDER POL-RD-03. The LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-00111-01) closes the PIE towards Tuas between Clementi Rd and Jalan Anak Bukit — the expressway segment the booked route uses — from 07:10 to 09:30, bracketing the 07:47:40–08:25:40 trip well inside the 15-minute buffer. The trace shows the vehicle leaving the corridor at Bukit Panjang, before the closed segment, and rejoining it after. The cap on that exoneration is 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km, and the measured excess of 5.98 km sits under it, so the whole excess is justified and no residue is left for a POL-RD-02 refund to operate on. Run the arithmetic against the closure-adjusted optimal (24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km, duration scaled to 37.5 minutes): recomputed fare is SGD 37.585 (3.80 base + 22.485 distance + 10.50 time + 0.80 platform fee, no ERP), against the 37.74 charged. The 0.155 difference is below the 0.50 de minimis, so the outcome is NO_ACTION.\n\nON THE RIDER'S OBJECTION that the route rejoins on the AYE and not on the PIE: we do not accept it. Both routes finish at one-north, which is served by the AYE, so the AYE carries the route to its destination and the rejoin there is a rejoin of the route the optimal follows after the closed segment; POL-RD-03(c) requires the vehicle to leave before the closed segment and rejoin after, which is what the trace shows. That reading is confirmed by the driver taking the authority's own posted diversion — 'Diversion via Upper Bukit Timah Rd' — and by his 29.98 km being essentially the advisory's shortest lawful alternative of 29.2 km. The rider's alternative arithmetic (recomputed fare 31.00, refund 6.74 rounded to 6.75) would be the figure if the exoneration failed, but it does not fail, so that figure does not operate here.\n\nPOL-RD-04 IS NOT IN PLAY. The rider gave no instruction to take any particular road, both waypoint_hint fields are null, and 'as long as I reach by 8.30' identifies no place; the driver did not rely on a rider-requested detour and the excess is not excluded on that footing. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00111) is used only as contemporaneous notice that the driver told the rider of the closure before completing the diversion, and the driver's account is consistent with the advisory.\n\nNO PASS-THROUGH CORRECTION ARISES. The fare breakdown records 0.00 of ERP and an empty gantry list, and the trace crosses no gantry, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to refund and its 12.00 cap is not reached. No repeat-deviation pattern is engaged under POL-RD-06 (0 flags in 90 days over 588 completed trips), so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral follows. No profile field below weight or outside POL-GEN-01's citable list was used. Every artifact here carries weight_multiplier 1.0, so no discount applies and the confidence floor is not breached. Because payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, the rider continues to pay the 37.74 — NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute leaves the charge as it stands; it does not re-create it. No clause in this case produces a referral, and no amount is held."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the deviation is established, but it is fully exonerated, so the fare that was charged stands and no refund issues.\n\nRider — you are right that the trip ran longer than booked. EV-GPS-00111 records 29.98 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 24.0 km: an excess of 5.98 km, or 24.9%, which crosses both POL-RD-01 gates (over 20% and over 0.8 km), and the trip record, trace and fare breakdown all carry TRP-00111 with the same 07:47:40 start. But the driver was not taking a shortcut of his own choosing. EV-ADVIS-00111-01 is a live LTA DataMall closure — a lorry fire, all lanes closed on the PIE towards Tuas between Clementi Rd and Jalan Anak Bukit — on the very corridor the booked optimal route uses, with a 07:10–09:30 window that brackets the whole 07:47–08:25 trip. The trace shows the vehicle leaving that corridor before the closed stretch (off the BKE at Bukit Panjang) and rejoining the route after it (on the AYE), which is the POL-RD-03(c) pattern, and the driver took the authority's own published diversion ('Diversion via Upper Bukit Timah Rd'). Your point that the rejoin was on the AYE rather than the PIE carriageway does not defeat the clause: the stretch being avoided was closed, so the rejoin can only be downstream.\n\nThe exoneration is capped at 1.30 x (29.2 - 24.0) + 1.00 = 7.76 km. The measured excess of 5.98 km is inside that cap, so the whole excess is justified, and POL-RD-03 sets the closure-adjusted optimal at 24.0 + 5.98 = 29.98 km, 37.5 min. Running POL-RD-02 on that adjusted route: recomputed fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 29.98 + 0.28 x 37.5) x 1.0 surge + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 37.585, against a charged total of 37.74. The difference is SGD 0.155, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so no refund issues and the recorded charge stands (payment status CHARGED, refund issued 0.00). The alternative arithmetic you offer (recomputed 31.00, difference 6.74) runs against the booked optimal, and POL-RD-03 directs POL-RD-02 to run against the closure-adjusted one instead.\n\nDriver — nothing further is owed to you either. No ERP or toll was charged (tolls_erp 0.00, no gantries on either route), so POL-RD-09 has nothing to settle, and there is no unbilled-distance shortfall, so POL-RD-04 compensation does not arise. The deviation is not MATERIAL (24.9% and 5.98 km are below the 50% and 8.0 km thresholds) and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across 588 completed trips, so no POL-RD-06 driver-conduct referral arises either.\n\nOn the remaining points: POL-RD-04 does not run — the chat log holds only the driver's 07:54:20 notice, which the rider read and answered, with no waypoint requested — and both sides agree it cannot excuse anything. The rider's additional-corroboration rule is not engaged (deviation_claims_60d is 1, below 4). Every artifact in this pool carries weight 1.0, so no finding is discounted. The rider is correct that NO_ACTION leaves the charge in place; that is the outcome because, once the closure is allowed for, the fare charged matches the fare the trip should have cost."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
